    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84). **Yordan Alvarez** is our clear priority start, benefiting from a massive matchup against a high-xERA opponent (20.25), while **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a high-ceiling park factor (+14%) and significant platoon advantage. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first strategy; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.71) is a priority plug, leveraging an elite lead-off spot (+10%) and an aggressive dynamic platoon edge to offset the potential threat posed by a quick-to-the-plate catcher. **Trea Turner** (68.27) remains essential in our 5x5 build, as his matchup against Eisert allows him to exploit a slow delivery profile, maximizing our stolen base potential in a category where we remain hyper-vigilant.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nelson Velazquez** (55.59) was the most difficult call of the day. Despite an elite xwOBA of 0.478, **Nelson Velazquez** was sidelined because the efficiency of our active outfield\u2014specifically the platoon-heavy upside of **Luke Raley** (62.89) and the stability of **Kyle Schwarber** (65.99)\u2014offered a more reliable path to hitting our daily game caps. While **Casey Schmitt** (50.51) also presented a compelling case due to his leadoff upside and stolen base potential against Brown, he ultimately fell short of the projected output of **Colt Keith** (51.62) and **Chase Meidroth** (51.61). We are closely monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (41.79) as the day\u2019s most marginal starter; his sub-42 score reflects a difficult matchup against Miller, making him the most likely candidate to be pulled if we reach our threshold caps early. Otherwise, the roster is set, though we must keep a sharp eye on any late weather updates in the East Coast games.",
